Remaining unburdened is more important than either speed or jumping.
If you're going to be burdened, speed boots are better than jumping--
likewise, if you're going to keep eating when you're satiated, an
amulet of unbreathing is better than reflection.  If you're playing
intelligently, though, neither of those situations should come into
play.

> =A0 =A0 =A0With the right spells, you can be both very fast and able to
> jump at the same time, having the best of both worlds.

Yep.  In practice, I often have haste self or blessed potions of speed
to use on Astral/Air/Sanctum/etc.  If not, though, I'd much rather
have only jumping boots than only speed boots--and if I'm going to
burn a wish on boots it'll be for jumping.

My primary objection is to the claim that "But the specific question
speed boots vs. jumping boots has a clear answer: speed boots";
there's certainly no clear answer there, though my impression is that
more top players tend to opt for jumping (though not uniformly), at
least in the late game.  Even early on, speed may more passively help
your chances, but jumping are more likely (IMO) to get you out of a
jam--and to me, having lots of "outs" is one of the keys to maximizing
my ascension %.  It's definitely a point where reasonable minds can
differ, though.


